- Within a `sextant` block, named for the instrument which reads a position, successive calls
- to `unpack` read one value after another. The position advances by the width of each value:
+ Dentro de un bloque `sextant`, llamado así por el instrumento que lee una posición, las llamadas
+ sucesivas a `unpack` leen un valor tras otro. La posición avanza según la anchura de cada valor:

= to `unpack` read one value after another. The position advances by the width of each value:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val version = data.sextant:
+ val version = data.sextant:

-   val magic = unpack[B32]
+   val magic = unpack[B32]

-   unpack[U16]
+   unpack[U16]

=   unpack[U16]
- ```
+ ```

- Binary formats favor repeated sections, and an array of records is unpacked by its count. The
- result of `unpack[Array[Pair]]` is a function from the count to the array, so the array is read
- once the count is known:
+ Los formatos binarios suelen tener secciones repetidas, y un array de registros se desempaqueta
+ según su número de elementos. El resultado de `unpack[Array[Pair]]` es una función del número de
+ elementos al array, de modo que el array se lee una vez que se conoce ese número:

= once the count is known:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- case class Pair(left: U16, right: U16)
+ case class Pair(left: U16, right: U16)

- object Pair:
+ object Pair:

-   given debufferable: (Pair is Debufferable) = Debufferable.derived
+   given debufferable: (Pair is Debufferable) = Debufferable.derived

- val count = hex"00010002000300040005000600070008".sextant:
+ val count = hex"00010002000300040005000600070008".sextant:

-   val pairs = unpack[Array[Pair]](4)
+   val pairs = unpack[Array[Pair]](4)

-   pairs.length
+   pairs.length

=   pairs.length
- ```
+ ```

=   pairs.length
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

=   pairs.length
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

=   pairs.length
= ```
